WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:04.160
For a moment, we want you to cast your mind
back to your childhood.

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.720
A time when you weren’t as busy or burdened
with the pressures of life that come as you

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:09.520
grow up.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.800
When you were carefree and had your whole
life ahead of you, nothing but potential and

00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:15.920
opportunity.

00:00:15.920 --> 00:00:21.040
A simpler time, when the highest award you
could achieve wasn’t a grade or a promotion,

00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:25.840
but something as simple as your mom or dad
pinning a drawing you did to the door of the

00:00:25.840 --> 00:00:26.960
refrigerator.

00:00:26.960 --> 00:00:28.880
Oh, to be a kid again, right?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:33.040
Then again, maybe returning to younger days
is better left as a fantasy.

00:00:33.040 --> 00:00:38.560
It’s hard to imagine that something so pure,
so simple and wholesome as a drawing on the

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.480
fridge could ever be something dark, horrific
even.

00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:48.720
But then, you learn about SCP-683, and all
of a sudden returning to your childhood becomes

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:51.760
something you hope never happens.

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:57.840
SCP-683 is an anomaly with various parts to
it, so we’ll start with SCP-683-1.

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:04.400
At first glance, it looks to be just an ordinary
refrigerator; to be more precise, it’s actually

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:10.000
a 1953 Crosley Shelvador, for any of you fridge
experts out there who are curious about the

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.920
exact make and model of SCP-683-1.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:18.640
For everyone else, picture the refrigerator
that Indiana Jones hid inside to miraculously

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:21.680
survive a nuclear blast in Kingdom of the
Crystal Skull.

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:27.520
I don’t know about you guys, but I’m feeling
nervous already.

00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:32.080
Like we said, at first glance you’d struggle
to spot anything out of the ordinary about

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:37.120
this particular fridge, apart from maybe some
slight wear and tear on the outside.

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:42.560
Inside though, it’s perfectly clean, kept
in perfect working condition for keeping food

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:43.200
cool.

00:01:43.200 --> 00:01:47.280
But that’s the first weird thing about SCP-683-1.

00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:52.000
You see, despite the Foundation conducting
tests to deliberately make it messier, the

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:57.520
fridge seems to have an inbuilt function that
you wouldn’t find in one from Home Depot.

00:01:57.520 --> 00:01:59.520
It can self-clean.

00:01:59.520 --> 00:02:03.920
Yes, that doesn’t sound all that impressive
- unless you’re a fridge owner yourself

00:02:03.920 --> 00:02:06.640
and know what a nightmare they can be to keep
clean.

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:12.720
While it’s definitely weird, it’s not
the last of SCP-683-1’s anomalous properties.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:17.120
The next is the fact that the power cord of
this refrigerator ends with a plug that doesn’t

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.680
match any known type of wall outlet.

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:24.560
Seems even stranger, after all, who would
design a fridge that can’t even be plugged

00:02:24.560 --> 00:02:25.440
in, right?

00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:31.280
In fact, the SCP Foundation had to design
their very own completely one of a kind adapter

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.640
to connect SCP-683-1 to an ordinary gas-powered
home generator.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.640
Once plugged in though, SCP-683-1 functions&nbsp;

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:43.520
exactly like you would&nbsp;
expect any other refrigerator

00:02:43.520 --> 00:02:45.760
to… sort of.

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:53.280
It’s about time we move on to SCP-683’s
second component, designated as SCP-683-2.

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:58.160
Again, much like the fridge it is somehow
affixed to, at first look this part looks

00:02:58.160 --> 00:02:59.600
completely ordinary.

00:02:59.600 --> 00:03:04.400
It’s a drawing, created using felt pens
and pencils, presumably by a child between

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:06.960
the ages of five and seven years old.

00:03:06.960 --> 00:03:11.120
There’s evidence of some moderate water
damage to the paper, but once again nothing

00:03:11.120 --> 00:03:13.040
all that strange to look at.

00:03:13.040 --> 00:03:17.600
Even the subject of this child’s drawing
is pretty mundane, just some scribbles of

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:23.360
a pleasant mountainous landscape, a house,
a well, a dog, a figure wearing a chef’s

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:27.840
toque and, of course, an anthropomorphic sun
with a smiley face.

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:30.560
Now sure, that might not&nbsp;
sound all that impressive,&nbsp;

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.120
but we would advise not to say anything like

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.240
that out loud.

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:39.200
Criticizing the drawing is a comment you might
wish you hadn’t made, just like when you

00:03:39.200 --> 00:03:41.920
fill our comment sections with dated Among
Us memes.

00:03:44.240 --> 00:03:50.000
Any person that makes any kind of negative
or disparaging remark about the SCP-683-2

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:56.560
drawing, or tries to remove the paper from
the fridge door of SCP-683-1 will suffer a

00:03:56.560 --> 00:03:58.960
grim, horrific fate.

00:03:58.960 --> 00:04:04.000
The next time they try to eat anything, this
person will suffer immense, irreparable damage

00:04:04.000 --> 00:04:08.640
to their internal organs, along with their
skin and muscle tissue.

00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:14.720
This is intensely painful, causing the subject
agonizing pain as their organs and skin are

00:04:14.720 --> 00:04:15.840
melted down.

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:20.560
The amount the person loses is equal to the
mass of food they’ve eaten; with each bite,

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:22.960
they will lose more and more of their body.

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:28.640
The painful process will not stop until they
have ingested 0.42 kilograms of food.

00:04:28.640 --> 00:04:33.280
Making this even worse, the process doesn’t
seem to target any organs that would kill

00:04:33.280 --> 00:04:34.960
the subject immediately.

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:40.400
They’re made to suffer in excruciating pain,
punished with torture for daring to try and

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.800
remove the drawing from the fridge.

00:04:42.800 --> 00:04:48.320
Any and all subjects will die within twenty-six
days of taking that final bite and thus losing

00:04:48.320 --> 00:04:50.640
the last piece of themselves.

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.520
But, where do the body parts of these people
go?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:56.640
Surely, they don’t disappear, you must be
thinking.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:58.480
And you’d be right.

00:04:58.480 --> 00:05:04.960
In instances like this, the mystery third
component of SCP-683 is revealed.

00:05:04.960 --> 00:05:14.080
Referred to as SCP-683-3, a brown paper lunch
bag will manifest inside the SCP-683-1 fridge,

00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:18.640
containing a grim and grizzly assortment of
meals.

00:05:18.640 --> 00:05:25.120
On every occasion, the bag contains a sandwich,
with a pretty disgusting filling: the flesh

00:05:25.120 --> 00:05:30.400
and viscera of the last person who dared to
criticize the drawing on the refrigerator.

00:05:30.400 --> 00:05:35.360
There is also a plastic ziploc bag, in which
you’ll find the other half of the stolen

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:40.880
organs and flesh of this unlucky person, along
with three chocolate chip cookies.

00:05:40.880 --> 00:05:46.240
Surprisingly, these are actually completely
normal cookies with no traces of DNA or other

00:05:46.240 --> 00:05:48.000
abnormalities to them.

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:55.440
Every time, there is also one final item that
forms the contents of SCP-683-3, and that’s

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:59.040
a note which reads “Be a good boy today”.

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:03.920
This note bears the same handwriting as appears
on the outer surface of the paper bag, upon

00:06:03.920 --> 00:06:06.720
which a single name is written: Eric.

00:06:06.720 --> 00:06:11.600
Now, for those of you in the know about the
various anomalies of the SCP Foundation, that

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:15.600
particular, unassuming name might sound very
familiar.

00:06:15.600 --> 00:06:22.000
It was the same name mentioned by another
anomaly, known as SCP-066.

00:06:22.000 --> 00:06:27.680
A brief bit of context for you, SCP-066 was
a living ball of yarn that displayed friendly

00:06:27.680 --> 00:06:29.840
behavior towards Foundation staff.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:34.720
However, during an experiment, a thread was
cut from SCP-066’s body.

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:39.760
This caused the yarn to transform into a ball
of meat, with a pair of functional eyes protruding

00:06:39.760 --> 00:06:40.400
from it.

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:46.320
SCP-066 became hostile, constantly asking
for an ‘Eric’ whenever someone gets too

00:06:46.320 --> 00:06:47.200
close to it.

00:06:47.200 --> 00:06:53.360
The same name, Eric, was also found carved
into the back of SCP-168, another anomaly

00:06:53.360 --> 00:06:55.840
encountered by the SCP Foundation.

00:06:55.840 --> 00:07:01.600
SCP-168 was an anomalous calculator, which
actually possessed some level of sentience

00:07:01.600 --> 00:07:03.920
and had the ability to communicate.

00:07:03.920 --> 00:07:06.080
So, who is Eric?

00:07:06.080 --> 00:07:11.520
Well, theories range far and wide, but there’s
no real definitive answer as to exactly who,

00:07:11.520 --> 00:07:13.760
or what Eric might be.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:18.880
Some claim he’s a reality-bending entity,
others posit he’s an SCP that the Foundation

00:07:18.880 --> 00:07:20.640
just doesn’t know about yet.

00:07:20.640 --> 00:07:26.480
Regardless, he’s connected to some intriguing
entities; a sentient calculator, a formerly

00:07:26.480 --> 00:07:31.440
friendly ball of yarn, and a fridge with a
child’s drawing on it that can steal people’s

00:07:31.440 --> 00:07:35.440
organs and put them in a lunch bag especially
for him.

00:07:35.440 --> 00:07:41.040
It would seem that Eric is a child, maybe
a schoolboy, possibly even the one responsible

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:43.840
for the drawing on SCP-683.

00:07:43.840 --> 00:07:47.360
This child could even potentially be anomalous
in nature.

00:07:47.360 --> 00:07:52.560
Of course, this is all just rampant speculation
on our part, so it’s probably best to take

00:07:52.560 --> 00:07:54.560
all of that with a grain of salt.

00:07:54.560 --> 00:08:00.560
As we’ve said before, it’s just a theory
- an SCP Explained theory.

00:08:00.560 --> 00:08:06.240
Eric might just remain one of the Foundation’s
many unanswered mysteries for years to come.

00:08:06.240 --> 00:08:11.840
But if that answer doesn’t satisfy you,
then why don’t we go back to SCP-683.

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:17.120
Maybe something in the fridge’s origin will
give us a further clue to the mystery of who

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:18.320
Eric is.

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:23.040
The fridge was first discovered by the SCP
Foundation in the storage unit of a Washington

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:26.000
home, owned by a woman named Yolanda.

00:08:26.000 --> 00:08:31.440
As coincidence would have it, Yolanda was
a collector of vintage home furnishings, including

00:08:31.440 --> 00:08:35.760
refrigerators, which would probably explain
why she didn’t think to throw out such an

00:08:35.760 --> 00:08:38.720
old model of fridge from the 1950s.

00:08:38.720 --> 00:08:44.560
According to her, she found SCP-683 simply
left on a nearby street corner, with nobody

00:08:44.560 --> 00:08:48.640
around that could have left it there, or anyone
that could have possibly been transporting

00:08:48.640 --> 00:08:50.160
it to the local dump.

00:08:50.160 --> 00:08:54.960
To give her a hand moving the fridge, Yolanda
enlisted the help of her nephew, who agreed

00:08:54.960 --> 00:09:00.000
to step in and assist her in getting SCP-683
back to her house.

00:09:00.000 --> 00:09:05.040
Unfortunately, though, the nephew passed away
only two weeks later, apparently due to medical

00:09:05.040 --> 00:09:09.600
complications that came as the result of a
hernia according to his death certificate.

00:09:09.600 --> 00:09:13.680
Could Yolanda’s nephew have been the mysterious
and elusive Eric?

00:09:13.680 --> 00:09:17.680
Could something have happened to him after
his death that allowed him to become some

00:09:17.680 --> 00:09:19.040
kind of anomaly?

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:25.040
Who’s to say, we can only guess and hope
that one day we might get a full answer.

00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:30.480
As to why Yolanda never suffered the effects
of SCP-683, she never actually tried to take

00:09:30.480 --> 00:09:34.160
the SCP-683-2 drawing down from the fridge.

00:09:34.160 --> 00:09:38.400
When asked why, she simply replied “It’s
a nice little picture, isn't it?

00:09:38.400 --> 00:09:39.760
Why take it down?”

00:09:39.760 --> 00:09:45.040
Maybe, just maybe, it might have even reminded
her of her nephew.

00:09:45.040 --> 00:09:49.840
It would have been a futile and foolish idea
for Yolanda to have even tried to remove the

00:09:49.840 --> 00:09:55.600
drawing at any rate, as any who try will suffer
that painful and horrifying process of losing

00:09:55.600 --> 00:09:59.520
their organs and having them appear in Eric’s
paper lunch bag.

00:09:59.520 --> 00:10:04.880
Even fire can’t remove the drawing from
the fridge, at least not permanently, suggesting

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:09.360
that even the paper it is drawn on has its
own anomalous properties.

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:16.320
On three separate occasions, the SCP Foundation
has attempted to test this, setting SCP-683-2

00:10:16.320 --> 00:10:18.800
on fire with nothing more than a match.

00:10:18.800 --> 00:10:24.480
Every time, the drawing was incinerated, burned
to ashes until there was nothing left.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:31.200
But, within sixty-eight hours, SCP-683-2 had
returned to its permanent fixture on the fridge

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:33.920
door, as if nothing had happened.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:38.000
Interestingly though, the D Class members
of personnel that were instructed to burn

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:43.440
the drawing didn’t suffer the usual anomalous
effects of SCP-683.

00:10:43.440 --> 00:10:49.280
A similar thing happens if multiple people
attempt to remove SCP-683-2 or say anything

00:10:49.280 --> 00:10:50.960
negative towards the drawing.

00:10:50.960 --> 00:10:56.000
In cases like this, only the very first person
who made a disparaging remark, or tried to

00:10:56.000 --> 00:11:01.040
rip the drawing from the fridge will be the
one to suffer a long, painful torture by organ

00:11:01.040 --> 00:11:04.320
removal, followed swiftly by death.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:08.480
Now, if you cast your mind back to earlier
in the video, we told you that someone who

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:15.040
tries removing or disparages SCP-683-2 will
only suffer an anomalous lack of organs when

00:11:15.040 --> 00:11:16.640
they next eat something.

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:22.400
So, you must be thinking that the way to avoid
that is to simply not eat, to fast, and not

00:11:22.400 --> 00:11:24.080
ingest a single meal.

00:11:24.080 --> 00:11:28.640
And yes, you’d be right, that does stave
off the anomalous effects of the fridge and

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:34.160
the drawing, but also means you’re heading
towards an even slower, painful death from

00:11:34.160 --> 00:11:35.360
starvation.

00:11:35.360 --> 00:11:40.240
To date, two different Foundation test subjects
have died this way by refusing to eat after

00:11:40.240 --> 00:11:42.880
interacting with SCP-683.

00:11:42.880 --> 00:11:47.760
True, the SCP Foundation is most likely sitting
on a whole cavalcade of different anomalies

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:52.880
that can keep a person alive without the need
for food, but you know what they’re like,

00:11:52.880 --> 00:11:53.520
right?

00:11:53.520 --> 00:11:58.400
The Foundation’s hardly likely to share
the keys to surviving without having to eat.

00:11:58.400 --> 00:12:02.560
And there you have it, folks, that’s SCP-683.

00:12:02.560 --> 00:12:05.920
Don’t worry, it’s highly unlikely that
you’ll ever encounter it.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:11.360
The Foundation keeps it under lock and key,
in a cell fitted with a steel door and reinforced

00:12:11.360 --> 00:12:12.320
hinges.

00:12:12.320 --> 00:12:18.000
SCP-683 remains covered in a large cloth to
prevent any members of personnel from looking

00:12:18.000 --> 00:12:22.320
at it when the fridge isn’t being used for
research or experiments.

00:12:22.320 --> 00:12:27.760
But you have to wonder, what if it’s not
the only fridge with these anomalous properties?

00:12:27.760 --> 00:12:33.280
After all, it’s rare for a manufacturer
to make just a single refrigerator of a certain

00:12:33.280 --> 00:12:34.000
model.

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:38.400
Maybe you’d better be wary next time you
visit someone with an older model of fridge

00:12:38.400 --> 00:12:44.960
in their kitchen, and just to be safe, if
there’s a drawing pinned to the front door,

00:12:44.960 --> 00:12:46.560
leave it where it is.

00:12:46.560 --> 00:12:52.240
Now go check out “Killer Living Graffiti
SCP-1155 - Predatory Street Art” and “Living

00:12:52.240 --> 00:12:58.640
Drawing SCP-085 - Hand Drawn Cassy” for
more art that really jumps off the page!

